\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {30}{\ignorespaces 64 KiB puts, c16: aggregate rate / retained-final node count. Even spread assumed for callers, rate and payload; these are normalizations, not observed node-level metrics. Native: one process, one SSD. Tidehunter: five owners. Other external contributors record five configured or observed storage nodes; Cassandra's 3 November run records five contacts, not a verified five-node ring. Five storage-host SSD mounts are attested only for the inspected 4 November and final deployments. FoundationDB excludes its separate log/coordinator host. Rates use finite case time, including work outside API calls. Native: per-put file/directory barrier; TH: covering sync; Valkey: AOF-always; Garnet: AOF commit; Kvrocks: synced WAL. Other writes have unverified device persistence. No cache drop; coordinator cache off. Native and Tidehunter: one run on the full-matrix fleet; other stores: median over 2 to 6 GCP runs (different fleets, days, binaries). c1 is mixed, not pure-write.}}{27}{table.caption.47}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:pernode}{{30}{27}{64 KiB puts, c16: aggregate rate / retained-final node count. Even spread assumed for callers, rate and payload; these are normalizations, not observed node-level metrics. Native: one process, one SSD. Tidehunter: five owners. Other external contributors record five configured or observed storage nodes; Cassandra's 3 November run records five contacts, not a verified five-node ring. Five storage-host SSD mounts are attested only for the inspected 4 November and final deployments. FoundationDB excludes its separate log/coordinator host. Rates use finite case time, including work outside API calls. Native: per-put file/directory barrier; TH: covering sync; Valkey: AOF-always; Garnet: AOF commit; Kvrocks: synced WAL. Other writes have unverified device persistence. No cache drop; coordinator cache off. \runs . c1 is mixed, not pure-write}{table.caption.47}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {31}{\ignorespaces Individual 64 KiB c16 successful-put API p50 values, recomputed from raw samples; 4{,}096 puts per population. B: Native per-put all-file/directory barrier, one process/SSD. P: Native page-cache acknowledgement, no per-put foreground fsync or per-put persistence guarantee. S: owner verbs synchronous covering persistence, five owners. V: Valkey RDMA AOF-always. Cache state is not controlled; coordinator cache is off in the distributed KV cases. N3: 3 November campaign; M: full matrix; R7/R8: focused fleets. R8 K/N/W are different profiles, not extra independent repetitions; columns retain each profile's repetition index. O/D: 4 November manual read/delete exports; Q: queue campaign. Copied baselines in manual exports are not proved independent fleets. Full case ids, sample/archive paths and contracts are in \texttt  {spike-cases.csv}. No populations are pooled.}}{29}{table.caption.48}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:spike}{{31}{29}{Individual 64 KiB c16 successful-put API p50 values, recomputed from raw samples; \N {B:spike-cases:M_0379-native-65536-write-concurrent-primary_rf1-r0:n|,.0f} puts per population. B: Native per-put all-file/directory barrier, one process/SSD. P: Native page-cache acknowledgement, no per-put foreground fsync or per-put persistence guarantee. S: owner verbs synchronous covering persistence, five owners. V: Valkey RDMA AOF-always. Cache state is not controlled; coordinator cache is off in the distributed KV cases. N3: 3 November campaign; M: full matrix; R7/R8: focused fleets. R8 K/N/W are different profiles, not extra independent repetitions; columns retain each profile's repetition index. O/D: 4 November manual read/delete exports; Q: queue campaign. Copied baselines in manual exports are not proved independent fleets. Full case ids, sample/archive paths and contracts are in \texttt {spike-cases.csv}. No populations are pooled}{table.caption.48}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {32}{\ignorespaces Local structure test: transcribed from the audit report; raw samples not retained. Each cell lists IEEE run 1; run 2 separately; -- means not measured. Fresh mapping, \texttt  {MAP\_POPULATE}, write-prefault, \texttt  {pwrite} and anonymous memory have no per-put foreground persistence guarantee. Write-prefault writes every page and data-syncs before timing; \texttt  {MAP\_POPULATE} is not that control. Data sync means per-put \texttt  {fdatasync}; grouped sync is a covered-ticket model. Neither is the engine's complete file-and-directory barrier. Finite-case rates are not capacity estimates; per-call occupancy cannot be checked without retained samples. Source and run labels are in \texttt  {local-structure-test.csv}.}}{30}{table.caption.49}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:local-structure}{{32}{30}{Local structure test: transcribed from the audit report; raw samples not retained. Each cell lists IEEE run 1; run 2 separately; -- means not measured. Fresh mapping, \texttt {MAP\_POPULATE}, write-prefault, \texttt {pwrite} and anonymous memory have no per-put foreground persistence guarantee. Write-prefault writes every page and data-syncs before timing; \texttt {MAP\_POPULATE} is not that control. Data sync means per-put \texttt {fdatasync}; grouped sync is a covered-ticket model. Neither is the engine's complete file-and-directory barrier. Finite-case rates are not capacity estimates; per-call occupancy cannot be checked without retained samples. Source and run labels are in \texttt {local-structure-test.csv}}{table.caption.49}{}}
